File: wave.info, Node: mirror, Next: latest, Prev: linkquery, Up: Top


Show the address each kind of data is fetched from, including the
built-in defaults for anything not overridden by an environment
variable.

  --json
      Print the configuration as JSON

  --yaml
      Print the configuration as YAML

  --toml
      Print the configuration as TOML

  --raw
      Print export lines

  --only-set
      With --raw: export only the sources you overrode (the
      LINUXWAVE_*_DOMAIN variables), leaving the rest to the built-in
      defaults

  --show-password
      Print the real password

  --hide-user
      Hide the user name

Examples:

     wave mirror
     wave mirror --raw
     wave mirror --json
     wave mirror --show-password


File: wave.info, Node: latest, Next: basedir, Prev: mirror, Up: Top


Compare what you have with the newest version in the index; nothing is
downloaded.

  -a, --all
      Check every installed package

  --max-time <string>
      Maximum total time for one request (40s, 1min)

  --connect-timeout <string>
      Maximum time for the handshake

  --content-time <string>
      Maximum time to receive data

  -v, --verbose
      Print each request as it is made

